From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SwitchVN <switchvn@example.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: fix WoW64 demuxer destroy parameters

wow64_demuxer_destroy() allocated demuxer_create_params before passing it to
demuxer_destroy(). The create structure stores the demuxer after two pointers,
while the destroy structure stores it at offset zero, so the Unix side read an
uninitialized handle and dereferenced a null demuxer during graph teardown.

Use the matching destroy parameter structure so the native demuxer and its
stream context are released correctly when a 32-bit game closes an ASF graph.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c b/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c
index 29dfba72c90..c362690b917 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ static NTSTATUS wow64_demuxer_destroy( void *arg )
         struct winedmo_demuxer demuxer;
         PTR32 context;
     } *params32 = arg;
-    struct demuxer_create_params params;
+    struct demuxer_destroy_params params;
     NTSTATUS status;
 
     params.demuxer = params32->demuxer;

-- 
